# Declared patch-coverage toolchain — what CI's `patch-coverage` job installs.
#
# EDIT THIS FILE, then run `python3 scripts/lock_toolchain.py` to regenerate the
# hash-pinned `coverage-tools.txt` beside it.
#
# Self-contained for the same reason as mutation-tools.in: one hashed file per
# consumer, never two layered at install time.
#
# Resolved for Python 3.12 — the version CI's patch-coverage job pins.
#
# That job no longer runs the suite (it downloads the ubuntu-3.12 `tests`
# cell's coverage.xml), so it needs only diff-cover; the test toolchain still
# comes along through `-r test-tools.in`, which is cheaper than a second lock.
-r test-tools.in
diff-cover
